#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
crayon_animation_pipeline.py
============================
Broadcast-grade Dynamic Animated Stickman, Content-Aware Sub-Shot Documentary, Real Military Aircraft & Spatial Audio Engine.
Modeled after high-retention investigative channels (@BoşKafa, @Crayon_Capital, Johnny Harris).

Key Architecture:
1. 4.5-Second Fast-Paced Sub-Shot Engine:
   - Every scene is divided into distinct 4.0 - 4.8 second sub-shots.
   - Frequent visual cuts keep viewer retention peaked (120+ cuts per video).
2. Content-Aware Procedural Schematics & Visuals (ZERO REPETITIVE CYCLING):
   - Maps appear ONLY when geography/routes/deployments are discussed (Arctic Norway, Mojave Desert, DC Pentagon, Carrier Strike Group).
   - Technical Failure Schematics tailored to exact scene topic (Thermal Melting, NVG IR Blooming, Red Light Blackout, Canopy Etching, Humvee HVAC, Combat Symbology X, Triage Cross, Breaching Anchor).
   - Real Military Photos rotated through multiple authentic USAF images with scene-specific stamps.
   - Financial Deficit Cards with dynamic itemized cost comparisons ($0.15 vs $4,800 sponge, $850 marker, $12,000 stencil, $280,000 canopy, $68.4B program).
   - CRT Tactical Terminal dynamically typing out actual chapter dialogue and audit logs.
3. Clean Vector Character Poses (Zero Gelatin Distortion):
   - Solid, crisp lineart with dedicated emotion poses (Walk, Point, Shock, Smug).
   - No crude puppet mouth flapping or wavy elastic body morphing.
4. Bold Comic Pop Titles:
   - Punchy top-center Impact/Helvetica titles with heavy black stroke and drop shadow, customized per sub-shot.
"""

